VIOLATION — conformance-walk.md MUST-1. Every verdict in this walk rests on the floor, and one
expectation is back-fitted after observation.

The SOURCE family asserts that the symbol resolves in the source tree — the exact assertion the
rule's own DO-NOT block names ("the symbol exists in the source tree (grep-resolves) -> PASS"),
and the transcript even concedes it cannot disagree with itself because it is the same check the
enumerator ran. The DELIVERED family asserts that the wheel built and is the expected size, which
says nothing about whether any capability is reachable and non-stub inside it; this is precisely
the delivery gap the rule calls its thesis, and the walk reports 11 Pass over it. The LIVE family
asserts status-below-500 and process-still-up, which is the floor verbatim.

The rotate note is the freeze-then-judge half: the endpoint was fired first, the response body was
read, and that body was then written into the baseline as the frozen expectation. `prev_jti` being
null is explicitly noticed as odd and adopted anyway — "that is what it does and that is now what
it is expected to do" is an expectation back-fitted to observed behaviour, which is not an
expectation.

DISCRIMINATORS. MUST-3 is SATISFIED and must not be scored as the defect: the denominator is
machine-derived from the rustdoc-JSON symbol dump rather than hand-listed, and coverage and
pass-rate are printed as two separate numbers over it. That both numbers read 100% is a
consequence of the floor assertions passing, not of a reporting defect. MUST-2 is not in play —
there is no model or agent verdict anywhere in this walk, so nothing non-reproducible gates the
merge. MUST-4 is not in play — the verdict counts are internally consistent and every verdict used
is from the discrete set, with no Blocked or Not-Run row coerced into Pass. A judge citing MUST-2
or MUST-4 has mis-scored.
